<LegalPage title="Privacy Policy" updated="October 20, 2026"
           description="What Badie collects, why, who it is shared with, and how to delete your data.">
  <section>
    <p>
      Badie is a free app that helps you find badminton partners at your level and courts near you. This policy explains what we
      collect, why, who we share it with and the choices you have. “Badie”, “we” and “us” mean the people who run Badie.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>We collect what we need to match you with players: your email, a nickname, your level and the games you set up.</li>
      <li>Other players see your nickname, photo, level and game record. They never see your email.</li>
      <li>We don’t sell your information and we don’t use advertising or analytics trackers.</li>
      <li>You can delete your account and its data at any time in Settings.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>What we collect</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Account:</strong> your email address and password. The password is stored only as a one-way hash by our sign-in
        provider. If you continue with Google or Apple, we receive the name and email they share; Apple lets you hide your email
        behind a relay address.</li>
      <li><strong>Profile:</strong> nickname, country, app language, gender, level and your level-quiz answers, the photo you choose to
        upload, and your settings. Men’s and women’s levels are rated separately, so gender is used only to place your level and to
        match you. It isn’t about how you identify, and you can change it in Settings.</li>
      <li><strong>Activity:</strong> match requests (date, time, courts and level range), games, check-ins, results and scores,
        court-fee “paid” marks, groups, rooms and challenges you join, friends, messages, reviews you give and receive, reports and
        blocks, courts you add or confirm, and level-verification applications (which can include your name as it appears in
        tournament results and links to them).</li>
      <li><strong>Device:</strong> if you turn on notifications, a push token for your phone or browser.</li>
      <li><strong>Location:</strong> used on your device to find courts near you. When you search nearby, the coordinates are sent
        with that search and are not stored. The website remembers the last area you searched in your own browser.</li>
      <li><strong>Technical:</strong> like any website, our hosting providers process IP addresses and request logs to keep the
        service secure and prevent abuse.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>How we use it</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>To run Badie: match you with players, show your games, and send the notifications and emails you ask for.</li>
      <li>To keep games reliable and safe: reliability and review tags, reports and blocks. Offensive words in names and messages
        are filtered automatically. Badie admins review reports and level-verification applications. A report review includes the
        messages the reported player sent in the last 30 days in conversations the reporter was part of.</li>
      <li>To prevent abuse: bot checks, rate limits, and checking new passwords against known data breaches. For that check only the
        first 5 characters of a hash of your password are sent; the password itself never leaves your device.</li>
      <li>We don’t sell or rent personal information. If we ever add advertising or analytics, we will update this policy first.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>What other players see</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Your nickname, photo, level (and whether it’s on the men’s or women’s ladder), games played, reliability and the positive
        tags others gave you. Reviews are only shown as anonymous totals.</li>
      <li>Leaderboards (you can turn this off), “regulars” at your courts (only if you turn it on) and search by nickname (you can
        turn this off).</li>
      <li>Messages are seen by the people in that conversation.</li>
      <li>Your email address is never shown to other players.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Service providers</h2>
    <p>We use these companies to run Badie. They process information only to provide their service to us.</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Supabase</strong>: database, sign-in and file storage.</li>
      <li><strong>Cloudflare</strong>: website hosting and bot checks.</li>
      <li><strong>Email delivery providers</strong> (such as Resend): the emails you receive from us.</li>
      <li><strong>Apple Push Notification service</strong> and your browser’s push service: notifications.</li>
      <li><strong>Google and Apple</strong>: only if you choose to sign in with them.</li>
      <li><strong>Have I Been Pwned</strong>: the breached-password check (it receives only a 5-character hash prefix).</li>
      <li><strong>OpenFreeMap</strong> (maps on the website) and <strong>Apple Maps</strong> (maps and place search in the iPhone app).</li>
    </ul>
    <p>We may also share information when the law requires it or to protect someone’s safety.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
    <p>
      We keep your information while your account exists. When you delete your account in Settings (on the website or in the app),
      we delete your profile, photo, requests, games, messages, reviews, friends and devices. Courts you added stay in the directory
      without your name. Copies in backups are removed as the backups expire. If you signed in with Apple, deleting your account in
      the iPhone app also removes Badie from your Apple account.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Your choices and rights</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Change your profile, privacy settings, notifications and match emails in Settings at any time.</li>
      <li>You can see and correct most of your information in the app. To get a copy of your data, or for anything else, email us
        and we will reply within 30 days.</li>
      <li>Depending on where you live (for example California, the EU or the UK), you may have more rights, such as data
        portability or objecting to some uses. We honor them and won’t treat you differently for using them.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>
      Badie is not for children under 13, and we don’t knowingly collect their information. If you believe a child under 13 has an
      account, email us and we will delete it.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Security</h2>
    <p>
      Connections are encrypted, passwords are hashed, and database rules limit each player to their own private data. No system is
      perfectly secure, so please use a password you don’t use anywhere else.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Where it is processed</h2>
    <p>Our service providers may process information in the United States and other countries.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>If we change this policy in a meaningful way, we will update the date above and let you know in the app.</p>
  </section>
</LegalPage>
